== a_number_on_an_axis_of_categories
note: 1 row with NA in shop or units dropped (line 2)
error[Z0401]: the plot places `shop` as categories along `x`, but `units`, which `points` maps to `x`, is an Int, which is placed on a linear scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:46
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop, y: units).points().points(x: units)
  |                                              ^^^^^ `units` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one axis, so what is mapped to `x` must all be categories (a Str or a Category), all be numbers or all be dates (a Date or a DateTime); `category(v)` makes categories of a number

== categories_on_a_linear_axis
error[Z0401]: the plot places `units` on a linear scale along `y`, but `shop`, which `lines` maps to `y`, is a Str, which is placed as categories
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:46
  |
2 | d.plot(x: units, y: units).points().lines(y: shop)
  |                                              ^^^^ `shop` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one axis, so what is mapped to `y` must all be categories (a Str or a Category), all be numbers or all be dates (a Date or a DateTime); `category(v)` makes categories of a number

== an_expression_on_an_axis_of_categories
