  = help: the layers of a plot share one axis, so what is mapped to `x` must all be categories (a Str or a Category), all be numbers or all be dates (a Date or a DateTime); `category(v)` makes categories of a number

== a_frame_that_holds_the_category_as_a_number
error[Z0401]: `points` places `x` as categories, so `shop` of this frame must be a Str or Category variable, but it is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:40
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop, y: units).points(data: frame(shop = [1, 2], units = [3, 4]))
  |                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ its `shop` is not categories
  |
  = help: the plot maps `shop` to `x` as categories, so the frame of every layer must hold it as categories; `category(shop)` makes categories of a number

== a_frame_that_holds_the_number_as_text
error[Z0401]: `points` draws `x` on a linear scale, so `units` of this frame must be a Bool, Int or Float variable, but it is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:41
  |
2 | d.plot(x: units, y: units).points(data: frame(units = ["a", "b"]))
  |                                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ its `units` is not numeric
  |
  = help: the plot maps `units` to `x`, so the frame of every layer must hold it as a number

